{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git diff --stat; cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794416392000-engineer-cc3-fix-r10.glm-5.3.findings.md; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc | sed -n '1295,1385p'\"","aggregated_output":" src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc               | 276 +++++++++++++++++++----\n test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc | 425 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n test/yin/repl/index_test.cljc        |  34 +++\n test/yin/repl/query_test.cljc        |  31 +++\n 4 files changed, 724 insertions(+), 42 deletions(-)\n## cc3 fix round r10 — the render-hook bypass (astra r9 F1 residue, final known gap)\n\nWorktree `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3`, branch `cc3-lowering-provenance`, HEAD `0ec036d1` + uncommitted r7+r8+r9 fixes, now + r10. Nothing committed.\n\nDeliverable mirror: the requested path under `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/` is outside this session 's writable roots, so this file is the mirror at `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/collab/yang-clojure/1794416392000-engineer-cc3-fix-r10.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md` (per the prompt 's mirror-and-say-so clause, r9 precedent). Written by glm-5.3, continuing the lane it authored r9 on.\n\n### The gap — the frontend `:render` hook executes outside both authoritative wrappers\n\nAstra r9-confirm accepted r9 with ONE residue: a supported frontend `:render` hook runs at repl.cljc:1326 inside `finalize-eval`, AFTER `run-evaluator-stage` returns — so its throw crosses neither r9 wrap site, yet still lands in a recovery catch:\n\n- immediate completion: `run-evaluation` catches it at ~:2054 and merges the payload 's `::call-provenance-handles` (~:2080) and prefers its `::call-provenance-failures` over `@latest` through `retention-recovery-failures` (~:334) — fabricated handles, a fabricated diagnostic, and a fabricated Warning in the throwing round itself.\n- pending completion: `recheck-pending*` renders at ~:2526 and its catch adopts the carried fields at ~:2560 — the forged vector REPLACES the session 's genuine diagnostics, the forged handle merges in, and because the recheck path has no `with-index-notice`, the fabricated round-failures surface one round LATE as a Warning on the next input.\n\n### Probe (red first)\n\nA scratch namespace (deleted before delivery) drove both regions against the pre-fix r9 code, with the standard Clojure frontend re-installed over a host catalog whose binding carries an armed `:render` hook that throws the same forged payload as r9 (`:forged/admission` failure + `\"forged-handle\"`), with `r9-refusing-store` for a genuinely-failing variant:\n\n- immediate: after two healthy def rounds, the render round `(+ (g) 1)` answered `Error: renderer boom` PLUS `Warning: this round 's call provenance was not retained (relation write failed: forged retention failure)`; failures = the forged vector; handles = 2 genuine + the round 's own real handle + `\"forged-handle\"`.\n- pending: `(require (quote mod))` parked behind a withholding content source (the require round genuinely claims: +1 handle at park); the completing `recheck-pending` over a serving source answered `Error: renderer boom` alone, but the session held the forged diagnostic and handle, and the NEXT round (`42`) answered `42` + the fabricated Warning.\n\nAlso resolved empirically: the probe programs claim (the immediate render round +1 handle, the require park round +1 handle), which fixes the exact survival counts the tests assert.\n\n### Fix — the shell snapshot rides the render raise too (`src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc` only)\n\nThe r9 mechanism, extended to the one remaining host-code execution point inside the protected operation. `finalize-eval` 's render call (repl.cljc:1331) is now wrapped: any raise from the hook is re-thrown as `(ex-info <same message> (assoc <original ex-data> ::call-provenance-handles/:failures/:round-failures <the keys on state#>) <original cause>)` — the session state 's own retention record, the snapshot the evaluator stage already merged before finalize runs, assoc 'd UNCONDITIONALLY over whatever the hook payload carried (nil = the empty snapshot, which still overwrites a forged value; the recovery gates ' `or` then fall through to the same shell-owned `@latest`/session values). Message, cause, and every other ex-data key (the observer `:session`, link identity) pass through unchanged, so error text and rollback semantics are byte-identical for a genuine renderer failure.\n\nOne site covers all three finalize callers — run-evaluation 's two (immediate halt, post-drive-links halt) and recheck-pending* 's pending completion. With it, every exception that can reach a recovery catch crosses one of three wrap sites (evaluator-stage, link-raise, finalize/render); the two catches ' reads are shell-owned on every path, and the catch bodies are UNCHANGED (a short comment at each names the three wraps). The php frontend 's `:render :php/out` keyword hook is unaffected: keyword lookup cannot throw, and non-throwing renderers never enter the wrap.\n\n### Tests (astra spec: immediate + pending-completion renderer, conflicting exception data)\n\n`test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc`, beside the r9 tests: the forged payload extracted to `r9-forged-evidence` (shared with `r9-forged-boom`), `r9-assert-no-fabricated-evidence` parameterized by error prefix (its two r9 call sites unchanged in behavior), plus new helpers `r10-forged-renderer` (armed gate, renders plainly unarmed) and `r10-render-catalog` (Clojure frontend + `:render` via `yang.frontend`), and the require-path machinery (closed module, publisher, withholding source) local per require-test 's pattern:\n\n- `repl-fabricated-retention-evidence-is-ignored-from-the-renderer-test` — immediate, doseq healthy/genuine: reuses the r9 contract wholesale on the render throw (`Error: renderer boom`): no fabricated diagnostic/handle/Warning; healthy — zero failures, no false Warning, the round 's own handle survives exactly once (+1); conflicting (r9-refusing-store) — the genuine `:relation` admission-scoped failure survives exactly once with its Warning exactly once, handles equal the earlier set.\n- `repl-fabricated-retention-evidence-is-ignored-on-pending-completion-test` (JVM-gated like the r4 link-resume sibling) — parks `(require (quote mod))` behind a withholding source with the armed renderer staged on the run, completes it via `recheck-pending` over a serving source: the completing round reports the renderer error alone; the park round 's genuine Warning (exactly once, when its retention really failed) stays where it was; no forged diagnostic or handle ever enters the session; every advertised handle is a real segment address; completed handles survive exactly once; and the FOLLOW-UP round answers `42` alone — the late fabricated Warning (the pre-fix leak 's observable) is gone.\n\nRed-first evidence: against the pre-fix code the two tests fail with 24 failures (13 immediate + 11 pending, both variants each) — fabricated diagnostics, false Warning (in-round and one-round-late), forged handle merged; after the fix, 0.\n\n### Verification\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Probe, pre-fix (immediate / pending) | false Warning + forged handle + forged diagnostic in-round; pending: forged diagnostic replaces the genuine set, late Warning on the next round |\n| Probe/test, post-fix | clean on all four variants; genuine refusal still warns exactly once, at park |\n| New r10 tests, pre-fix code | 2 tests / 57 assertions, **24 failures** |\n| New r10 tests, fixed | 2 / 57, **0 failures** |\n| ` clojure -M:test -n yang.clojure-callsite-test -n yin.repl.index-test -n yin.repl.query-test` | 88 tests / 1141 assertions, **0 failures** (r9: 86/1084) |\n| ` clojure -M:test -n yin.repl.index-test -n yin.repl.query-test -n yin.repl-test -n yin.repl.store-test -n yang.clojure-callsite-test` | 167 / 1541, **0 failures** (r9: 165/1484) |\n| ` clojure -M:test -n yin.repl.index-test -n yin.repl.query-test -n yin.repl-test -n yin.repl.store-test -n dao.stream.ws-project-cross-node-test` (r7 net) | 126 / 1015, **0 failures** (unchanged, as at r9; cross-node ns CLJS-only, not exercised on JVM) |\n| ` clj -M:kondo --lint src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc test/yin/repl/index_test.cljc test/yin/repl/query_test.cljc` | **0 errors, 0 warnings** |\n| Full ` clojure -M:test` | PENDING-ROW |\n\nFrozen contracts re-proven green by the rows above: the r8 F4 selective-write tests and the r3/r4 handle-survival tests (immediate and link-resume) inside `yang.clojure-callsite-test`, both r9 forgery tests unchanged in contract (helper parameterization only), the F3-confirmed stage-tagging paths (`retention-throw`, `with-index-notice`, `retention-notice` untouched this round), and the additive Warning contract (no new round-text surface; the only Warning text remains the r8 line). Forbidden files untouched: `semantic.cljc` and `observer.cljc` are not in the diff; the fix lives entirely in `repl.cljc`. The three clj-only test requires are reader-gated (kondo cljc clean, 0 warnings).\n\nDiff on top of the uncommitted r7+r8+r9 state: `src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc` (the finalize-eval render wrap + docstring + two catch comments) and `test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc` (forged-evidence extraction, helper parameterization + 2 call-site updates, r10 helpers + 2 deftests, gated requires). Commit: none, as instructed.\n  1295\t(defn- commit-frontend\n  1296\t  \"Keep what a frontend program's lowering staged (`::frontend`, see\n  1297\t   `eval-compiled`) now that its VM state survives: the frontend session\n  1298\t   it leaves becomes the shell's `:frontend-session`.\"\n  1299\t  [state]\n  1300\t  (let [staged (::frontend state)]\n  1301\t    (cond-> (dissoc state ::frontend)\n  1302\t      (contains? staged :session) (assoc :frontend-session (:session staged)))))\n  1303\t\n  1304\t\n  1305\t(defn- finalize-eval\n  1306\t  \"Drain the round's output and its result from the output medium.  Only a\n  1307\t   result stamped with this round's identity is this round's value; the\n  1308\t   evaluator answers once per halted program, after its prints.  The\n  1309\t   render hook is host code executing at the round's very end,\n  1310\t   after every retention wrap site, so a raise from it is re-wrapped\n  1311\t   with the session's own retention snapshot (empty included)\n  1312\t   before it can reach a recovery catch.  A missing\n  1313\t   or foreign-round result is loss, reported with the append outcome the\n  1314\t   runner recorded.  The program halted, so its VM state survives and a\n  1315\t   frontend's staged session is committed; a frontend with a `:render`\n  1316\t   shows its value as that renders it, the loop printing for every language.\"\n  1317\t  [state state' vm']\n  1318\t  (let [append (::result-append vm')\n  1319\t        render (:render (::frontend state'))\n  1320\t        [state'' output-text results]\n  1321\t        (drain-output (commit-frontend\n  1322\t                        (assoc state' :vm (dissoc vm' ::result-append))))\n  1323\t        round (round-id state')\n  1324\t        current (filterv #(= round (:round %)) results)]\n  1325\t    (if (seq current)\n  1326\t      (let [value (:value (peek current))]\n  1327\t        [(record-last-value state state'' value)\n  1328\t         (str output-text\n  1329\t              (if render\n  1330\t                (try\n  1331\t                  (render value)\n  1332\t                  (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) error\n  1333\t                    ;; r10 (astra r9 F1 residue): this hook runs AFTER\n  1334\t                    ;; run-evaluator-stage returns -- outside both r9\n  1335\t                    ;; wrap sites -- yet still inside the round recovery\n  1336\t                    ;; try, so its raise is re-wrapped with the shell\n  1337\t                    ;; snapshot of this round: the retention keys the\n  1338\t                    ;; session state already records (the empty\n  1339\t                    ;; snapshot included) are assoc-ed unconditionally\n  1340\t                    ;; over whatever the hook payload carried.  Every\n  1341\t                    ;; exception that can reach a recovery catch now\n  1342\t                    ;; crosses one of the three wrap sites, so recovery\n  1343\t                    ;; never reads retention evidence from a frontend\n  1344\t                    ;; hook either.\n  1345\t                    (throw (ex-info (or (ex-message error) (str error))\n  1346\t                                    (assoc (or (ex-data error) {})\n  1347\t                                           ::call-provenance-handles\n  1348\t                                           (:call-provenance-handles state'')\n  1349\t                                           ::call-provenance-failures\n  1350\t                                           (:call-provenance-failures state'')\n  1351\t                                           ::call-provenance-round-failures\n  1352\t                                           (:call-provenance-round-failures\n  1353\t                                             state''))\n  1354\t                                    error))))\n  1355\t                (format-value value (host-fn-namer (:vm state'')))))])\n  1356\t      [state''\n  1357\t       (str output-text \"Error: \" result-loss-text\n  1358\t            (when (and append (not= :dao.stream/ok append))\n  1359\t              (str \" (append: \" (name append) \")\")))])))\n  1360\t\n  1361\t\n  1362\t(defn- drain-observer\n  1363\t  \"Advance one observer past every batch still on its medium, keeping any\n  1364\t   gap it recovers across.  A nil observer — a session without that medium —\n  1365\t   stays nil.\"\n  1366\t  [observer]\n  1367\t  (when observer\n  1368\t    (loop [observer observer]\n  1369\t      (let [{:keys [status] observer' :observer}\n  1370\t            (observer/observe-next observer)]\n  1371\t        (if (#{:ok :gap} status) (recur observer') observer')))))\n  1372\t\n  1373\t\n  1374\t(defn- ingress-gaps\n  1375\t  \"Gaps the evaluation path's observers counted.  The code indexer's are\n  1376\t   its own: an index loss is reported without refusing evaluation.\"\n  1377\t  [state]\n  1378\t  (+ (:ingress-gaps (:observer state) 0)\n  1379\t     (:ingress-gaps (:row-observer state) 0)))\n  1380\t\n  1381\t\n  1382\t(defn- consume-failed-round\n  1383\t  \"Answer a round that threw with a recoverable shell state.\n  1384\t\n  1385\t   The failed input is consumed exactly once: each of the session's\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git diff -- test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc | tail -305; rg -n 'catch|finalize-eval|link-raise|run-evaluator-stage|retention-recovery|call-provenance-handles d|call-provenance-failures d' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"+        (is (= :relation (:stage (first failures))))\n+        (is (some? (:admission (first failures)))\n+            \"the surviving diagnostic is admission-scoped\")\n+        (is (str/includes?\n+              text \"relation write failed: store refused the provenance write\")\n+            \"the genuine Warning is still reported\")\n+        (is (= 1 (count (re-seq #\"call provenance was not retained\" text)))\n+            \"the Warning appears exactly once, not duplicated by the merge\")\n+        (is (= handles-before handles)\n+            \"no incomplete handle; earlier completed handles survive\"))\n+    (do (is (empty? failures)\n+            \"healthy retention records no failure\")\n+        (is (not (str/includes? text \"call provenance was not retained\"))\n+            \"the false Warning is not generated\")\n+        (is (= (inc (count handles-before)) (count handles))\n+            \"this round completed handle survives exactly once\"))))\n+\n+\n+\n+(deftest repl-fabricated-retention-evidence-is-ignored-test\n+  ;; cc3 r9 F1: a guest/host throw carrying fabricated\n+  ;; :yin.repl/call-provenance-* keys is not retention evidence. The\n+  ;; shell snapshot (empty included) is authoritative on the wrap the\n+  ;; evaluator stage makes, so no fabricated diagnostic, handle or\n+  ;; Warning appears, while genuine retention — completed handles, and\n+  ;; a real store refusal — survives exactly once.\n+  (doseq [[label genuine-failure?] [[\"healthy retention\" false]\n+                                    [\"genuine retention failure\" true]]]\n+    (testing label\n+      (let [fail? (atom false)\n+            [s1 _] (repl/eval-input\n+                     (repl-frontends/create-state\n+                       {:index-store (r9-refusing-store fail?)\n+                        :primitives {(quote boom) r9-forged-boom}})\n+                     \"(def k (fn [] 1))\")\n+            [s2 _] (repl/eval-input s1 \"(def g (fn [] (+ (k) 41)))\")\n+            handles-before (repl/call-provenance-handles s2)]\n+        (is (seq handles-before) \"precondition: earlier retention completed\")\n+        (is (empty? (repl/call-provenance-failures s2))\n+            \"precondition: retention was healthy so far\")\n+        (reset! fail? genuine-failure?)\n+        (let [[s3 text] (repl/eval-input s2 \"(+ (g) (boom))\")]\n+          (r9-assert-no-fabricated-evidence\n+            \"Error: guest boom\"\n+            genuine-failure? text (repl/call-provenance-failures s3)\n+            (repl/call-provenance-handles s3) handles-before))))))\n+\n+\n+(deftest repl-fabricated-retention-evidence-is-ignored-on-link-resume-test\n+  ;; cc3 r9 F1: the same forgery in a throw the shell raises while\n+  ;; resuming a query wait (the link-raise path through drive-links)\n+  ;; is not retention evidence either: the raise carries the shell\n+  ;; snapshot unconditionally over the wrapped payload, so no\n+  ;; fabricated diagnostic, handle or Warning appears, while genuine\n+  ;; retention survives exactly once.\n+  (doseq [[label genuine-failure?] [[\"healthy retention\" false]\n+                                    [\"genuine retention failure\" true]]]\n+    (testing label\n+      (let [fail? (atom false)\n+            s1 (reduce (fn [s line] (first (repl/eval-input s line)))\n+                       (repl-frontends/create-state\n+                         {:index-store (r9-refusing-store fail?)\n+                          :primitives {(quote boom) r9-forged-boom}})\n+                       [\"(def k (fn [] 1))\"\n+                        \"(def g (fn [] (+ (k) 41)))\"\n+                        \"(require (quote dao.space.query))\"])\n+            handles-before (repl/call-provenance-handles s1)]\n+        (is (seq handles-before) \"precondition: earlier retention completed\")\n+        (is (empty? (repl/call-provenance-failures s1))\n+            \"precondition: retention was healthy so far\")\n+        (reset! fail? genuine-failure?)\n+        (let [[s2 text] (repl/eval-input\n+                          s1\n+                          (str \"(let [r (dao.space.query/q \"\n+                               \"(quote [:find (count ?e) . \"\n+                               \":where [?e :yin/name ?n]]))] (boom))\"))]\n+          (r9-assert-no-fabricated-evidence\n+            \"Error: guest boom\"\n+            genuine-failure? text (repl/call-provenance-failures s2)\n+            (repl/call-provenance-handles s2) handles-before))))))\n+\n+\n+(defn- r10-forged-renderer\n+  \"A frontend :render hook whose throw fabricates retention evidence\n+   (cc3 r10, astra r9 F1 residue): the hook executes AFTER\n+   run-evaluator-stage returns, outside both r9 wrap sites, and only\n+   while `armed? is set; unarmed it renders the value plainly, so a\n+   session's earlier rounds render through untouched.\"\n+  [armed?]\n+  (fn [value]\n+    (if @armed?\n+      (throw (ex-info \"renderer boom\" r9-forged-evidence))\n+      (str value))))\n+\n+\n+(defn- r10-render-catalog\n+  \"The Clojure frontend with a `:render` hook installed (cc3 r10): a\n+   session over this catalog shows every halting round value through\n+   the hook — the supported frontend seam `finalize-eval` calls after\n+   the evaluator stage returns.\"\n+  [render]\n+  (frontend/install frontend/empty-catalog\n+                    (repl-frontends/clojure-manifest)\n+                    {:input :forms\n+                     :parse identity\n+                     :lower (fn [forms]\n+                              (if (= 1 (count forms))\n+                                (yang/compile (first forms))\n+                                (yang/compile-program forms)))\n+                     :render render}))\n+\n+\n+(deftest repl-fabricated-retention-evidence-is-ignored-from-the-renderer-test\n+  ;; cc3 r10 (astra r9 F1 residue): a frontend :render hook executes\n+  ;; after run-evaluator-stage returns — outside both r9 wrap sites —\n+  ;; and a throw from it reaches run-evaluation's recovery catch\n+  ;; directly. The render raise carries the shell snapshot (empty\n+  ;; included) over whatever the hook payload claimed, so no\n+  ;; fabricated diagnostic, handle or Warning appears, while genuine\n+  ;; retention — completed handles, and a real store refusal —\n+  ;; survives exactly once.\n+  (doseq [[label genuine-failure?] [[\"healthy retention\" false]\n+                                    [\"genuine retention failure\" true]]]\n+    (testing label\n+      (let [fail? (atom false)\n+            render-armed? (atom false)\n+            [s1 _] (repl/eval-input\n+                    (repl-frontends/create-state\n+                     {:frontends (r10-render-catalog\n+                                  (r10-forged-renderer render-armed?))\n+                      :index-store (r9-refusing-store fail?)})\n+                    \"(def k (fn [] 1))\")\n+            [s2 _] (repl/eval-input s1 \"(def g (fn [] (+ (k) 41)))\")\n+            handles-before (repl/call-provenance-handles s2)]\n+        (is (seq handles-before) \"precondition: earlier retention completed\")\n+        (is (empty? (repl/call-provenance-failures s2))\n+            \"precondition: retention was healthy so far\")\n+        (reset! fail? genuine-failure?)\n+        (reset! render-armed? true)\n+        (let [[s3 text] (repl/eval-input s2 \"(+ (g) 1)\")]\n+          (r9-assert-no-fabricated-evidence\n+            \"Error: renderer boom\"\n+            genuine-failure? text (repl/call-provenance-failures s3)\n+            (repl/call-provenance-handles s3) handles-before))))))\n+\n+\n+#?(:clj\n+   (defn- r10-closed-module\n+     \"require-test closed corpus module, local: one export, one\n+      retained free name — the module a parked require links on every\n+      backend the shell supports.\"\n+     []\n+     {:type :application\n+      :operator {:type :variable, :name (quote yin/def)}\n+      :operands [{:type :literal, :value (quote f)}\n+                 {:type :lambda, :params []\n+                  :body {:type :application\n+                         :operator {:type :variable, :name (quote +)}\n+                         :operands [{:type :literal, :value 40}\n+                                    {:type :literal, :value 2}]}}]}))\n+\n+\n+#?(:clj\n+   (defn- r10-publish-module\n+     \"require-test publisher, local: publish `ast` as the module `name`\n+      in `store`, answering the manifest address a parked require\n+      links.\"\n+     [store ast name exports]\n+     (:address (publish/publish-module!\n+                 store {:name name :ast ast :exports exports\n+                        :requires {}\n+                        :primitives {(quote +)\n+                                     (get vm/primitives (quote +))}}))))\n+\n+\n+#?(:clj\n+   (defn- r10-withholding-source\n+     \"require-test withholding source, local: `comp` with a content\n+      request medium that never delivers a request for `address`, so a\n+      link whose manifest is `address` spends its budget and stays\n+      pending while every other link over the same source completes.\"\n+     [comp address]\n+     (let [wire (:dao.stream/handle\n+                 (ring/create! {:dao.stream/type ring/transport-type\n+                                ring/capacity-key 1024}))]\n+       (assoc-in comp [:content :requests]\n+                 (reify\n+                   stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n+                   (descriptor [_] (stream/descriptor wire))\n+\n+                   stream/IDaoStreamReader\n+\n+                   (cursor [_ anchor] (stream/cursor wire anchor))\n+\n+                   (next [_ c] (stream/ne