{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"The explicit render hook is wrapped correctly for all three callers. The default formatter is still outside that wrapper, though: a host primitive can return a lazy sequence that throws only when formatting realizes it. That exception reaches recovery unsanitized. The PHP hook is safe for its actual result map; “keyword lookup cannot throw” is too broad as a general claim.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794416392000-engineer-cc3-fix-r10.glm-5.3.stdout.log'\nwith open(p) as f:\n for i,l in enumerate(f,1):\n  if any(s in l for s in ['24 failures','57 assertions','24F','0 failures','pre-fix']): print(str(i)+': '+l[:1000].rstrip())\nPY\nnl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/effect.cljc | sed -n '1,62p'; git diff --check\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794416392000-engineer-cc3-fix-r10.glm-5.3.stdout.log'\nwith open(p) as f:\n for i,l in enumerate(f,1):\n  if any(s in l for s in ['24 failures','57 assertions','24F','0 failures','pre-fix']): print(str(i)+': '+l[:1000].rstrip())\nPY\nnl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/effect.cljc | sed -n '1,62p'; git diff --check\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.vm.effect\n     2\t  \"The in-machine effect value (D4).\n     3\t\n     4\t   An effect is a host type minted only by `make`, which is never a guest\n     5\t   primitive or module export. `effect?` is a type test, so an ordinary\n     6\t   map is always data, including a map carrying an `:effect` key: a\n     7\t   `:pure` primitive that returns guest data can no longer raise an\n     8\t   engine effect.\n     9\t\n    10\t   The type wraps a plain descriptor map, `{:effect kind ...params}`, and\n    11\t   answers keyword lookup over it, so handlers and park-entry builders read\n    12\t   `(:effect e)`, `(:val e)` and the rest unchanged. It is not a map: guest\n    13\t   `assoc` cannot extend it, and `map?` is false.\n    14\t\n    15\t   The wrapper is an in-machine value only. What crosses a stream or a\n    16\t   wire is the plain descriptor (`descriptor`) or the fields a handler\n    17\t   reads out of it, never the wrapper.\")\n    18\t\n    19\t\n    20\t(deftype Effect\n    21\t  [descriptor]\n    22\t  #?@(:cljd [cljd.core/ILookup\n    23\t             (-lookup [_ k] (get descriptor k))\n    24\t             (-lookup [_ k not-found] (get descriptor k not-found))\n    25\t             (-contains-key? [_ k] (contains? descriptor k))]\n    26\t      :clj [clojure.lang.ILookup\n    27\t            (valAt [_ k] (get descriptor k))\n    28\t            (valAt [_ k not-found] (get descriptor k not-found))\n    29\t            Object\n    30\t            (toString [_] (str \"#yin/effect \" (pr-str descriptor)))]\n    31\t      :cljs [ILookup\n    32\t             (-lookup [_ k] (get descriptor k))\n    33\t             (-lookup [_ k not-found] (get descriptor k not-found))]))\n    34\t\n    35\t\n    36\t(defn effect?\n    37\t  \"True when `x` is an effect value minted by `make`. A type test: no map\n    38\t   is an effect, whatever keys it carries.\"\n    39\t  [x]\n    40\t  (instance? Effect x))\n    41\t\n    42\t\n    43\t(defn make\n    44\t  \"Mint an effect of `kind` over the plain parameter map `params`. The one\n    45\t   trusted constructor; never register it as a guest primitive or export.\"\n    46\t  ([kind] (make kind nil))\n    47\t  ([kind params]\n    48\t   (Effect. (assoc params :effect kind))))\n    49\t\n    50\t\n    51\t(defn descriptor\n    52\t  \"The plain descriptor map `{:effect kind ...}` of effect `e`: the form an\n    53\t   effect takes at a stream or wire boundary.\"\n    54\t  [e]\n    55\t  (.-descriptor ^Effect e))\n    56\t\n    57\t\n    58\t(defn from-descriptor\n    59\t  \"Mint the effect a plain descriptor map `d` names. The trusted boundary\n    60\t   conversion for host code that holds a portable descriptor; never\n    61\t   applied to a value a guest computed.\"\n    62\t  [d]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-11-11 17:40:00 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-12 00:40:00 ICT\n\nF1: CONFIRMED-FIXED **for exceptions thrown by the explicit render hook**. The wrapper unconditionally overwrites all three retention keys from session state, including nil. It preserves unrelated ex-data and retains the original exception as its cause. All three finalization callers share this site. [repl.cljc:1330](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1330).\n\nF2: OBJECTION: **P1 — default result formatting still bypasses the wrappers.**\n\nThe fallback `format-value` call remains outside the new `try` at [repl.cljc:1355](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1355). It realizes sequences through `first` and subsequent traversal at [repl.cljc:639](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:639).\n\nA concrete remaining path is a host primitive returning:\n\n```clojure\n(lazy-seq (throw (ex-info \"late boom\" forged-retention-data)))\n```\n\nThe primitive returns normally; the VM accepts its result, and the output ring stores it without realization. Formatting later triggers the exception outside all three wrappers. See [semantic.cljc:201](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:201) and [ringbuffer.cljc:124](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/src/cljc/dao/stream/ringbuffer.cljc:124).\n\nRecovery consequently still merges fabricated handles and accepts fabricated failures at [repl.cljc:2112](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:2112). Pending recovery has the equivalent exposure at [2597](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:2597).\n\n**Required fix:** protect default formatting as well as explicit rendering, or make recovery obtain retention evidence exclusively from trusted shell-owned state. Add a regression where a primitive returns normally but its result throws during for